From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:59:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 65/79] server: a cut XML tool call's value drops the closer it
 began

When max_tokens cut a reply inside a <parameter=...> value, finishCut sent
the bytes it held back for the closer as argument text, so a cut that ended
on the closer's first tokens streamed them: agentshape2 mixed12k-s0-t1 sent
`echo \"no /work\"\n</` as the bash command's tail. A cut value now drops a
start of </parameter> at its end and the framing newline before it, as a
closed value drops its framing newline and as the GLM and DSML cuts already
drop their closers. Bytes the value wrote stay; finish_reason stays length.

Tests (test-tool-cut-host): the receipt's 63 answer tokens replayed as their
decoded bytes, one event per token, whole and streamed; cuts inside the
closer at each of its prefixes, typed and untyped; complete calls, the
receipt's included, unchanged byte for byte.
